# EXPECT: passes a 0-element literal list to its single parameter
# ouroboros#181, count 0: `g of []` binds g's single parameter to [] on the
# VM (measured: `type of b` is list, `len of b` is 0, rc 0) -- the same
# re-collection as `g of [a, b]`. The old zero-arg refusal said "the VM
# binds null", which is only true of `g of null`. Refused with the measured
# reason until the call-site pack is emitted.
define g(b) as:
    return len of b
print of (g of [])
